WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.140
In this video, you create a virtual machine network that puts virtual machines on VLAN one hundred of the management cluster network.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:11.730
Under Networks, Virtual Machine Networks, select Create.

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:16.050
Choose the namespace that the network belongs to.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:17.970
Give it a name.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:24.070
The type is L2VlanNetwork, a layer two network tagged with a VLAN ID.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:29.650
Keep Access mode, so each virtual machine interface carries this one VLAN.

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:32.720
Enter VLAN ID one hundred.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:40.690
Select the cluster network that carries the VLAN. Here it is mgmt, the management network.

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:43.150
Select Create.

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:52.910
The new network is listed with its type, VLAN ID, and cluster network. Virtual machines can now attach to it.

00:00:52.910 --> 00:01:00.969
Virtual machines can now use VLAN one hundred. Next, you create an overlay network that needs no VLAN on the switch.
